DataShifter interface contract
  Hook execution order with around/before/on_success/on_error
    executes hooks in correct order: around(before) -> before -> call -> around(after) -> on_success
    on_error is called when call fails (around post-yield skipped on exception)
  Invocation returns Axn::Result
    .call returns Axn::Result
    .call with kwargs returns Axn::Result
  Failure handling
    Axn::Failure message is accessible
    fail! raises Axn::Failure which is captured
  Result API
    Axn::Result.error
      creates a failed result with message
      sets exception on error result
    result.ok?
      returns true for successful execution
      returns false for failed execution
    Axn::Result.ok
      accepts exposures as keyword arguments
      creates a successful result without message
      creates a successful result with optional message
    result.exception
      is nil for successful execution
      contains Axn::Failure for fail! calls
      contains the original exception for raised errors
      can be re-raised by caller (run!-style behavior)
  Core action with expects
    uses default value when argument not provided
    allows overriding default value
    includes Axn module
    supports expects with type: :boolean and default:
  Lifecycle hooks
    executes before hook before call
    executes around hook wrapping call
    does not execute on_success when call fails
    executes on_success hook after successful call
    does not execute on_error when call succeeds
    executes on_error hook after failed call

